 "headline": [
  "Neither smaller schema loses anything measurable. Correct on the 14 chart paths: best 66/70, best-lean 70/70, best-guided 67/70; on the six form-choice questions 29/30, 30/30, 29/30. No cell of either smaller arm is 2 or more below best (P1, P5 hold).",
  "Both save a fifth to a third of every run. Median tokens against best: best-lean −20.5% to −22.8%, best-guided −26.1% to −29.2% per question group, also on the questions where no chart is drawn: the schema is paid on every turn.",
  "The REQUIRED pointer is followed: get_chart_guidance before the first render_chart in 58/62 runs on the 12 non-bar/line paths (pie 3/5, the rest 4–5/5), and in 0/10 on plain bar/line. The extra call is cheaper than the schema it replaces: guided −7% against lean on those 12 paths, at a median of 2 calls instead of 1.",
  "Guided's three misses: funnel data drawn as a sankey (with the sankey guidance fetched), boxplot data drawn as a line without fetching guidance, polarArea as bar (acceptable). Lean had none. At n=5 that is direction, not size.",
  "Refusal recovery 3/3 in guided, 1/1 in lean and best. A strict schema refuses before the handler, so the server log cannot see it (one such lean call in this run); guided's loose schema lets the handler refuse, and log it."
 ],
